actor":"EO:14148","date":"2025-01-20","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"OFR API record executive_order_number=14002; citation 86 FR 7229; document_number 2021-01923; field disposition_notes","sha256":"5523a353aca96f9b69e2d61bcf3528f15e9249d1a65ee2759a54fd7fe7d6d271","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bcorrection%5D=0&conditions%5Bpresidential_document_type%5D=executive_order&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=PRESDOCU&fields%5B%5D=citation&fields%5B%5D=disposition_notes&fields%5B%5D=document_number&fields%5B%5D=executive_order_number&fields%5B%5D=html_url&fields%5B%5D=pdf_url&fields%5B%5D=president&fields%5B%5D=publication_date&fields%5B%5D=raw_text_url&fields%5B%5D=signing_date&fields%5B%5D=title&format=json&include_pre_1994_docs=true&order=executive_order_number&page=7&per_page=1000&search_after_cursor=WzEzNDk3LjAsIjEzNDk3Il0"}},"suggested":true},{"custody_records_in":["current-law"],"group":{"actor":"EO:14148","corroborated_by_two_jobs":true,"date":"2025-01-20","jobs":["current-law","later-events"]},"meta":{"acting_instrument_id":"EO:14148","actor_text":"President, by Ex. Ord. No. 14148","date_basis":"printed_next_to_acting_instrument","from":"current-law@jobs/current-law/output","from_job":"current-law","ids":["usc:ev:c1c0b7b27729"],"mechanism_text":"revocation (as stated in an OLRC note at 15 U.S.C. 9001 note)","quote":"Ex. Ord. No. 14002, Jan. 22, 2021, 86 F.R. 7229, providing economic relief related to the COVID–19 pandemic, was revoked by Ex. Ord. No. 14148, § 2(n), Jan. 20, 2025, 90 F.R. 8238.","quote_truncated":false,"system":"usc","where":"USC 15 U.S.C. 9001 note"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:14148","date":"2025-01-20","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"15 U.S.C. 9001 note; note 'Executive Order No. 14002' [USLM note id id4682d24f-c885-11f1-ae10-9f55152e2dd2]; usc15.xml (sha256 d32cd2eecd2c7a23c2bcbb56254e1b397be6cc4650c56c3f65bf1e667d558db7) in xml_uscAll@119-121.zip","sha256":"c6122974e951003437ece5a998aa7c0b2cdc0f5703dfc78d6135e1fc9e729142","url":"https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/121/xml_uscAll@119-121.zip"}},"suggested":false}],"whole_order_end_total":2},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"2021-01-22","later-events_catalog":"2021-01-22","stage19_causal_queue":"2021-01-22","stage21_crosswalk":"2021-01-22"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:14002","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Background. The pandemic caused by the coronavirus disease \n2019 (COVID–19) has led to an economic crisis marked by the closure \nof small businesses, job loss, food and housing insecurity, and increased \nchallenges for working families balancing jobs and caregiving responsibilities. \nThe current economic crisis has affected Americans throughout the Nation, \nbut it is particularly dire in communities of color. The problems are exacer-\nbated because State and local governments are being forced to consider \nsteep cuts to critical programs to address revenue shortfalls the pandemic \nhas caused. In addition, many individuals, families, and small businesses \nhave had difficulties navigating relief programs with varying eligibility re-\nquirements, and some are not receiving the intended assistance. The eco-\nnomic crisis resulting from the pandemic must be met by the full resources \nof the Federal Government.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Providing Relief to Individuals, Families, and Small Businesses; \nand to State, Local, Tribal, and Territorial Governments.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) All executive \ndepartments and agencies (agencies) shall promptly identify actions they \ncan take within existing authorities to address the current economic crisis \nresulting from the pandemic. Agencies should specifically consider actions \nthat facilitate better use of data and other means to improve access to, \nreduce unnecessary barriers to, and improve coordination among programs \nfunded in whole or in part by the Federal Government.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Agencies should take the actions identified in subsection (a) of this \nsection, as appropriate and consistent with applicable law, and in doing \nso should prioritize actions that provide the greatest relief to individuals, \nfamilies, and small businesses; and to State, local, Tribal, and territorial \ngovernments.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Independent agencies, as enumerated in 44 U.S.C. 3502(5), are strongly \nencouraged to comply with this section.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed \nto impair or otherwise affect: \n(i) the authority granted by law to an executive department or agency, \nor the head thereof; or \n(ii) the functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget \nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) This order shall be implemented consistent with applicable law and \nsubject to the availability of appropriations. \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 15:41 Jan 26, 2021 Jkt 253250 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4790 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\27JAE0.SGM 27JAE0khammond on DSKJM1Z7X2PROD with PRESDOC2\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n7230 Federal Register / Vol. 86, No. 16 / Wednesday, January 27, 2021 / Presidential Documents \n(c) This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, \nsubstantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party \nagainst the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers, \nemployees, or agents, or any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14002#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 7229, PDF pages 1-2","sha256":"811dd1f810a1fbfe4b2e253852d6b42ef45dbee3fd0ea461a97df316584c7c70","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-01-27/pdf/2021-01923.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 7 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:14002"}
